# Enduo Fitatu Agent configuration. Copy to .env (never commit it). Nothing here is required.

# --- Enduo ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENDUO_URL=https://api.enduo.app
# Name of the container in Enduo, shown with its token (default: "Fitatu Agent (<hostname>)").
# ENDUO_CLIENT_NAME=
# A personal access token with the "write:food_log" scope instead of signing in with a code.
# ENDUO_TOKEN=

# --- Sync ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How often Fitatu is asked for the recent days, in seconds (at least 60).
# POLL_SECONDS=300
# Days read on every pass: today and the days before it.
# RECENT_DAYS=3
# Days read again once a day, for an older day edited later (0 turns it off).
# RECHECK_DAYS=14
# On the first run, send the diary of this many days back, BACKFILL_BATCH days per pass. 0 sends only the recent days.
# BACKFILL_DAYS=90
# BACKFILL_BATCH=14
# Which rows count as eaten: "auto" (the ticked rows of a day when it has any, else every row), "eaten" or "all".
# DIARY_ITEMS=auto
# Time zone of your days (default: the one of the Fitatu account).
# TIMEZONE=Europe/Warsaw

# --- Goal in Fitatu ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "on" sets the energy and macro targets of the day in Enduo as the daily goal in Fitatu, every pass (README, "Goal in
# Fitatu"). This changes the goal in your Fitatu settings; `enduo-fitatu targets --restore` puts yours back.
# TARGETS=off

# --- Fitatu (read through fitatu-api) -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by `enduo-fitatu setup` (it asks when they are not set). With both set, the container also signs in again by
# itself when Fitatu ends its session. Without them the password is used once and never stored.
# FITATU_EMAIL=
# FITATU_PASSWORD=
# Log level of fitatu-api and this agent on stderr (default WARNING).
# FITATU_LOG_LEVEL=WARNING
# When Fitatu changes its web app's version or key before a release of fitatu-api does, e.g. {"app_version": "4.14.0"}.
# FITATU_CLIENT_PROFILE=

# --- User-Agent ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to "enduo-fitatu-agent/<version> (+https://github.com/sklimaszewski/enduo-fitatu-agent)". The calls to Fitatu are
# made by fitatu-api, as its web client.
# ENDUO_USER_AGENT=
